@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the foreign-arch dependency tree is ALREADY detected and already isolated on docker — the gap is one Kit field proveo does not model on sbx
' status: proposed 2026-09-10, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: internal/sbx/kit.go (no Volumes field today)
' would touch: internal/run/run.go (StripDepCopies, the warning at ~660)
' would touch: internal/workspace/deps.go (DepCopy), internal/workspace/mount.go
'   the schema field this needs .... _spec/_experiments/sbx-kit-capabilities.puml (volumes[])
'   why sbx cannot mask a subpath .. _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml
'   why a clone sidesteps it ....... _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
'   why a tmpfs is not free ........ _spec/minimum_requirements.puml (no swap)
'   the OTHER answer to the same problem _spec/_experiments/reusable-clone.puml
'     — a reused clone keeps a NATIVE tree instead of shadowing a foreign one
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
'   THE CLASS THIS IS AN INSTANCE OF: _spec/_paradigms/workspace-boundary.puml
'     — direct mode imports the host's file semantics; a clone re-materialises
'     them. Presence, mode/ownership, architecture and which-tree are one cause
'     meeting four properties of a file. Keep only this file's distinct half.
'
' ── FIRST: ALMOST ALL OF THIS IS ALREADY BUILT ─────────────────────────────
' The request was to plan for detecting a foreign-arch `node_modules` and
' installing instead, and to ask whether that is even possible. It is possible,
' and it is done. Written down so nobody rebuilds it:
'
'   `_dep_probe`                 walks native binaries by per-language name
'                                pattern, caps the walk (PROVEO_DEPS_PROBE_LIMIT,
'                                60) and calls `_proveo_foreign_object` on each —
'                                an OBJECT-FORMAT check, not name matching — then
'                                names the owning package
'   `_dep_addons_tree`           on a foreign tree, explains the shape better
'                                than a plan would: "the portable majority still
'                                loads, so the failure arrives later, at the
'                                first call into one of them, naming the TOOL
'                                rather than the platform"
'   `_proveo_dep_is_isolated`    reads /proc/self/mountinfo to ask whether the
'                                tree is ITS OWN MOUNT — i.e. proveo's private
'                                copy rather than the operator's checkout
'   ownership decides            isolated -> clear and reinstall. The host's own
'                                tree -> REFUSE, and name two remedies:
'                                `--clone`, or `PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall` which
'                                rewrites the checkout and says so
'   `workspace.DepCopy`          on the DOCKER backend, dependency trees are
'                                isolated outright: "dependency trees isolated,
'                                host untouched"
'
' The refusal is the right call and should not be softened: installing Linux
' binaries into a macOS checkout trades a broken agent for a broken laptop.
'
' ── SO THE GAP IS ONE BACKEND, AND ONE FIELD ───────────────────────────────
' sbx is the exception, deliberately and visibly:
'
'   internal/run/run.go:658   `workspace.StripDepCopies(...)` removes the
'                             isolation mounts on the sbx backend
'   internal/run/run.go:660   and warns: "sbx mirrors the checkout, so its N
'                             dependency tree(s) (node_modules, target, .venv …)
'                             cross into the sandbox as the host built them"
'
' The reason is the one workspace-env-key.puml already records for `.env`: sbx
' takes DIRECTORY workspaces at their own host paths, so there has been nothing
' to hang a per-subdirectory overlay on.
'
' EXCEPT THE KIT SCHEMA LISTS ONE. sbx-kit-capabilities.puml, reading SPEC-v2,
' records `volumes[]  block or tmpfs, path + size` among what a Kit may declare.
' And `sbx.Kit` has NO Volumes field — proveo does not model it. So the
' capability may have been there the whole time and the isolation was ruled out
' by an assumption rather than by a probe.
'
' ── THE PROBE, AND IT IS ONE KIT ───────────────────────────────────────────
' Declare a `volumes[]` entry — tmpfs, sized — at `<workspace>/node_modules` in
' a `kind: sandbox` Kit, start a run whose workspace has a foreign
' `node_modules`, and ask two things:
'   DOES IT SHADOW?   is the mirrored host tree hidden by the volume, or does the
'                     directory mount win and the declaration do nothing?
'   IS IT ISOLATED?   does `_proveo_dep_is_isolated` then return TRUE for it —
'                     which is the existing signal that unlocks clear-and-
'                     reinstall with the host untouched
' A yes to both means the docker path already works here and only the model was
' missing.
'
' ── WHAT WOULD CHANGE, AND WHAT MUST NOT ───────────────────────────────────
' IF IT WORKS: `StripDepCopies` stops being necessary on sbx, the warning at
' run.go:660 turns from a fact of life into a fixed defect, and `--clone` stops
' being the only answer for a direct-mode workspace. Nothing downstream needs
' rewriting, because `_dep_addons_tree` already does the right thing the moment
' the tree reports as isolated.
'
' WHAT MUST NOT CHANGE: proveo still never rewrites the operator's checkout
' without `PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall`. A volume that shadows is not permission to
' install into a tree that does not.
'
' ── THE COSTS THAT COULD SINK IT ───────────────────────────────────────────
'   A tmpfs IS RAM, AND A SANDBOX HAS NO SWAP. minimum_requirements.puml records
'     that memory pressure in a sandbox does not degrade, it KILLS, with no
'     OOMKilled flag and no exit message. A monorepo's `node_modules` in tmpfs
'     is gigabytes of guest memory, so the size must be declared deliberately
'     and an overflow must fail legibly rather than as a mystery kill.
'   A BLOCK VOLUME PERSISTS. It survives the run, which reintroduces exactly the
'     staleness the host-wide secret store taught this tree to distrust: a tree
'     built for a lockfile nobody has any more.
'   SEVERAL TREES, NOT ONE. `node_modules`, `target`, `.venv` — the warning
'     already counts them, so whatever this becomes is per-tree and its cost
'     multiplies.
'
' ── STILL OPEN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' WHETHER A VOLUME CAN SIT INSIDE A MIRRORED DIRECTORY MOUNT AT ALL. That is the
' whole question and it is unmeasured. The `.env` case failed for a related
' reason and is the honest prior; a schema field is not a guarantee, as this
' tree has now learned twice — a pattern that PARSES is not a pattern that
' MATCHES (kit-domain-form.puml).
'
' WHETHER IT IS WORTH IT AT ALL, given `--clone` is already the sbx DEFAULT and
' already produces exec-correct, arch-correct trees. This only helps the
' operator who turned the default off, or whose workspace is not a repository.
' Measure who that is before building for them.
title PLANNED — the detection and the refusal are built;\nsbx isolation waits on one unmodelled Kit field

component "a foreign ""node_modules""\nbuilt on the host" as FOREIGN <<error>>
card "already built" as DONE <<host>> {
  component """_dep_probe""\nobject-format check, capped" as PROBE <<app>>
  component """_dep_addons_tree""\nexplains the delayed failure" as TREE <<app>>
  component """_proveo_dep_is_isolated""\nis it OUR mount?" as ISO <<app>>
}
component "docker: ""DepCopy""\nhost untouched" as DOCKER <<app>>
component "sbx: ""StripDepCopies""\nthe tree crosses as built" as SBXN <<error>>
component """volumes[]"" in the Kit schema\nNO ""Volumes"" field in sbx.Kit" as VOL <<error>>
component "the operator's checkout\nnever rewritten without\n""PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall""" as HOSTTREE <<error>>

FOREIGN ARROW_MAIN PROBE
PROBE ARROW_MAIN TREE
TREE ARROW_MAIN ISO : ownership decides
ISO ARROW_MAIN DOCKER : isolated -> clear + reinstall
ISO ARROW_ERROR HOSTTREE : the host's own -> REFUSE,\nname two remedies
SBXN ARROW_ERROR FOREIGN : no overlay to hang it on
VOL ARROW_OPTIONAL SBXN : the field that might\nclose it

note bottom of TREE
  **The message already beats the plan.** "The
  portable majority still loads, so the failure
  arrives later, at the first call into one of
  them, naming the TOOL rather than the
  platform." Nothing here improves on that.
end note

note bottom of HOSTTREE
  **The refusal is correct and stays.** Installing
  Linux binaries into a macOS checkout trades a
  broken agent for a broken laptop. A shadowing
  volume is not permission to write a tree that
  is not ours.
end note

note bottom of VOL
  **Ruled out by assumption, not by probe.**
  SPEC-v2 lists ""volumes[]"" — block or tmpfs,
  path and size — and ""sbx\.Kit"" models no such
  field. The capability may have been there the
  whole time.
end note

note right of SBXN
  **A tmpfs is RAM, and there is no swap.**
  Memory pressure in a sandbox kills without an
  OOMKilled flag. A monorepo's tree is gigabytes,
  so a size must be declared and an overflow must
  fail legibly.
end note

legend bottom
  **What is left to do, which is much less than it looks**
  ==
  **Nothing about detection.** ""_dep_probe"" already checks object format rather than
  names, ""_dep_addons_tree"" already explains the delayed failure, and ownership already
  decides whether to clear-and-reinstall or refuse. On docker, ""DepCopy"" already isolates.
  --
  **One probe**: declare a Kit ""volumes[]"" entry at ""<workspace>/node_modules"" and ask
  whether it shadows the mirrored tree AND whether ""_proveo_dep_is_isolated"" then reports
  it as ours. Yes to both means only the model was missing.
  ==
  **A schema field is not a guarantee.** The ""\.env"" case failed for a related reason, and
  this tree has twice learned that a pattern which PARSES is not one that MATCHES.
  --
  **And ask who it serves**: ""--clone"" is already the sbx default and already produces
  arch-correct trees, so this helps only the operator who turned it off or whose workspace
  is not a repository. Measure that population before building for it.
end legend
@enduml
